---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<Base title="Ice Hockey Shifts: Privacy" description="Privacy policy for the Ice Hockey Shifts iPhone app.">
  <section class="top narrow prose">
    <p class="meta kicker">Ice Hockey Shifts</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated 2026-11-13</p>

    <p>Ice Hockey Shifts (the phone app) does not collect any data. It has no account, no analytics, no
    advertising and no tracking, and it does not send anything over the internet.</p>

    <h2>What the app reads</h2>
    <p>The app reads activity files (<code>.fit</code>, or a <code>.zip</code> containing them) that you choose
    to open in it, usually exported from Garmin Connect after a game recorded with the Ice Hockey Shifts watch
    app. These files contain the activity's times, laps and heart rate.</p>

    <h2>Where it is kept</h2>
    <p>Imported games, the original files and your settings (position and how many players were dressed) are
    stored only on your phone, inside the app's own storage. Like other app data, they may be included in your
    device's iCloud or computer backup, depending on your backup settings.</p>

    <p>Removing a game in the app deletes it and its file from the phone. Deleting the app deletes everything
    it stored. Your watch and Garmin Connect keep their own copies.</p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>Nothing is shared with the developer or anyone else. The app does not use any third-party service that
    receives your data.</p>

    <h2>Health information</h2>
    <p>Heart-rate figures are shown for training interest only. The app is not a medical device and does not
    give medical advice.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The app collects no data from anyone, including children.</p>

    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with a new date. Questions:
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
